From b06a63d690447ed4613f5c2e6fbe80fef64df7f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michele Baldessari <mbaldess@redhat.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:40:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat: add wlr-data-control protocol binding and wl_seat
 support

Add the wlr-data-control-unstable-v1 Wayland protocol to the build and
bind both wl_seat and zwlr_data_control_manager_v1 globals in
PortalManager.

The wlr-data-control protocol allows privileged clients to manage
clipboard content on wlroots-based compositors (including Hyprland).
Combined with the wl_seat binding, this provides the foundation for
implementing clipboard sharing through the XDG Desktop Portal Clipboard
interface on InputCapture sessions.

The data control manager is bound at version 2 to support both regular
and primary selection. The seat is bound at version 7 (latest stable).
